And even if these hackers at these lower levels, you know, even if the people that are willing to hack on programs that have, you know, 1k crits or whatever are wrecking us, then how are we going to get wrecked when we start doing, you know, 10k crits or whatever.

564
00:47:16,140 --> 00:47:31,940
So I really liked that point, but I did also want to bring it around to something really insightful that I think you said, Keith, about how like the government should regulate whether or not we have bug bountying programs.

565
00:47:31,980 --> 00:47:40,920
And maybe this thing that Joel is talking about of like, we need to pay for bugs at a certain scale should be brought in at the federal level via regulation.

566
00:47:40,920 --> 00:47:46,520
And Keith, forgive me for not knowing this, but I know you live in America right now, but are you American as well?

